# Shell scripts are run straight out of the working tree by a Linux container
# (`just ci-linux`), so they have to keep their line endings whatever the host
# checks out with. `sh` reads a carriage return as part of the command and fails
# on the first line it meets one.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The two runtime libraries the graphics examples load, in the tree so a
# checkout builds without fetching anything. Said outright rather than left to
# content sniffing, since a line ending rewritten inside one is a library that
# will not load.
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.a binary
